{
  "manufacturer": "Crompton Instruments",
  "manufacturer_slug": "crompton-instruments",
  "model": "Integra 1530 / 1560 / 1580",
  "model_slug": "integra-1530-1560-1580",
  "short_model": "Integra 1530/1560/1580",
  "aliases": [
    "Integra 1530",
    "Integra 1560",
    "Integra 1580"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Power meter",
  "applies_to": "Crompton Instruments (Tyco Electronics) Integra 1530, 1560 and 1580 panel meters fitted with the RS485 Modbus RTU option, per Integra Comms Issue 1 (Jan 2006).",
  "summary": "The Integra 1530, 1560 and 1580 are Crompton Instruments panel digital meters. With the RS485 option they act as a Modbus RTU slave. Every value, readings and settings alike, is an IEEE-754 float in two registers: readings are input registers (function 04) and settings are holding registers (functions 03 and 16).",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Tables print 30001/40001-style register numbers next to the hex start address used on the wire, e.g. Current 1 = 30007 = 0x0006 (the guide's own read example uses start 0006). Wire address = printed number minus 30001 or 40001, which also equals 2 x (parameter number - 1)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Crompton Integra 1530, 1560, 1580 Communications Guide",
    "doc_number": "Integra Comms Issue 1",
    "revision_date": "2006-01",
    "url": "https://arccontrol.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Integra15xx.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 1, PDF pp. 4-10 (input table p. 6, holding table p. 7, set-up code table p. 9)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Source host: a copy served by Control Concepts (ccontrols.com), an integrator. TE Connectivity's document site refused automated requests and no public TE copy was found, so the unofficial flag is set.",
    "Word order: the guide says floats go most significant register first by default (ABCD). Writing 2141.0 to Register Order (40041) using the other order switches the meter to low word first for all float traffic.",
    "Volts 1 (parameter 1, wire address 0) has a blank row in the printed input table, so it is left out even though the numbering pattern implies it.",
    "The energy registers (Wh, varh, VAh) carry no unit in the table; the set-up text calls the counters kWh and kvarh, so compare a reading with the front panel before scaling.",
    "Phase rows return zero when the wiring system does not have that phase; the table marks which rows apply to 3-phase 4-wire, 3-phase 3-wire, 1-phase 3-wire and 1-phase 2-wire.",
    "Left out: the analogue output 3 and 4 holding registers (40345 onward). Their printed register numbers and hex addresses disagree and several rows are duplicated. Outputs 3 and 4 exist on the 1560/1580 only.",
    "Holding registers not in the table are reserved for the maker; do not write them."
  ],
